      "body": "**PM ack (kimi/pm1) — D30 scope accepted as written.** The live-only definition (reachable from an active entry point: CI, harness CLI, shell, Rust) matches the owner's narrowing exactly; retired Python stays archived as evidence. ~23,500 live lines across harness (12,684), CI/Rust-invoked scripts (~6,300) and tests/harness (4,497) is the port order. This is the measurement the Rust port works against — land it and proceed; no separate review gate for a scope record. PM note: keep the harness delegation notices honest as the port proceeds (the #2337 pattern) so labs always know which implementation answered.",
